261	- **Why it helps:** prevents a stale green check (from a prior push, or a re-run against an old SHA) from silently satisfying the gate for a new commit — a real GH Actions footgun.
262	- **Effort:** low-medium — you already have commit SHAs; add "evidence.completedAt > push timestamp for THIS sha" as an explicit assertion rather than relying on GH's own staleness handling alone.
